  <section class="individual text-left pb-3 pt-5">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A <span class="archetype">Caregiver</span>, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Hidden Qualities, Unknown Tendencies,<br>And Positive Attributes</span> That You Wouldn't Expect</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4">
              <img src="../assets/images/abilities.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>By nature, you are mostly a prudent thinker. Driven to deliver the best possible outcome for everyone else, you are calm and able to decide on a course of action that benefits all who come under your wing.</p>
              <p>Aside from that, you are also perceptive and react as the situation demands, never missing on social cues and any pitfalls that you need to look out for. You’ve got a beautiful heart-- and the brains to back it up.</p>
              <p>Generally, you <span class="text-orange">think of everything in a holistic way</span>. You don’t just try and save yourself in any problem; you try to figure things out for other people around you. Sometimes, it even works to your own detriment, but you don’t care for this one bit.</p>
              <p>Every kindness that you do for others is always a welcome thing, and the fact that you are willing to be the one to make sacrifices means that everyone will likewise care for you as a result.</p>
              <p>Though you are able to think of things from a logical perspective, you nevertheless favor a more intuitive approach to problem solving. To you, life has a lot of ways to be unpredictable and difficult to maneuver, and as such, you often need to rely on that gut feeling to tell you what your next moves will be. It doesn’t have to always make sense, but the fact that you’re willing to take calculated risks means that life often rewards you in huge ways.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Despite your preferences on gut-feeling and the impression it might give off, you’re actually quite <span class="text-orange">calm and able to control your emotions.</span> You don’t allow stress to get the best of you, and on the contrary you use stress as a motivator to push yourself to think in an even calmer way. The more you are able to assess situations in this objective light, the more you are able to help other people and keep your head in the game.</p>
          <p>That being said, there’s more about your potential than you understand at this juncture, <span class="username"></span>.</p>
          <p>With your hidden qualities in full view, it is time for you to know what your strengths are and how you can better use them...</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-1" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(1, 2)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step2">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A Caregiver, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Hidden Strengths And<br>Positive Attributes</span> That You Wouldn't Expect</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/abilities-2.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>Being a Caregiver, you are highly perceptive. Given your introvertness, understanding how things work naturally emanates from you. Whereas other people have a hard time figuring things out, you’ve already understood what’s going on. This allows you to ready to act, wasting little to no time in responding to the needs of others.</p>
              <p>Your perceptiveness usually reveals itself when it comes to emotional situations. Since you have a good grasp of how you feel and what you want to do, you usually don’t need to think twice when making a decision. Though you don’t express it, you are actually strong and firm-minded.</p>
              <p>As such, your perceptiveness manifests when you are coming to the aid of those around you. Like the Good Samaritan, you know what’s going on and why people aren’t coming to aid of the dying man. You can see one’s pain beyond their joyful exterior prompting you to do something and extend your time, treasure, and talents to alleviate the situation.</p>
              <p>Perceptiveness alone is not enough to move mountains. After all, being perceptive only means, you understand the situation and the underpinnings that surround it. What’s more important is empathy. Your ability to feel things out is truly what moves you to take action.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Generally, this stems from your we-centeredness. Because you <span class="text-orange">perceive the world from the lens of interconnectedness and union</span>, you understand the importance of each individual in the greater scheme of things. As such, you see your role as someone who provides the base and gives that much-needed boost to help others move forward.</p>
          <p>This is a gargantuan task, to say the least. Caregivers, much like the Hero archetype, needs to step beyond themselves to pursue the end that they want. At times, people may become disappointed or even annoyed by your empathetic stance but keep pushing since this is what makes you who you are.</p>
          <p>Additionally, you <span class="text-orange">possess that intuitiveness</span>. With it, you are trusting towards others. You actively open those walls to those around you and allow them to enter your inner circle. With the help of your own intuition, you don’t think twice about letting new people in, especially when they need your assistance.</p>
          <p>While this strength can be a double-edged sword (since others may betray you), your <span class="text-orange">trusting nature</span> allows you to truly extend your time, talents, and treasures to others. Whereas other people may simply do dole-outs or provide materially, your trust goes a long way and affects others intangibly.</p>
          <p>And because you have that inherent trust in you, you don’t quickly crumble from within. Whereas other archetypes rely on external validation, you are the type who simply relies on their own sense of goodness and morality. This carries you to new heights as you live out your mission in life.</p>
          <p>Finally, Emotional intelligence is often an underrated characteristic of existence. People, for instance, place a high premium on IQ over EQ. What most don’t know is that EQ is the base of one’s personality, allowing one to flourish in aspects that they seek.</p>
          <p>As a Caregiver, this is one of your biggest strengths. Due to your calmness, you are able to weigh things in properly. You do not panic. Instead, <span class="text-orange">you pause and take a step back</span>, thinking carefully what needs to be done to address a specific issue.</p>
          <p>Given such, you’re the type who can truly see what a person needs. With your ability to relate to others, you can connect with them in ways that will unravel how you can nurture them. In doing so, you can properly address their inner issues instead of simply placing temporary band-aid solutions.</p>
          <p>Now that you’re acquainted with your strengths, dear <span class="username"></span>, it is time for you to know how you can exercise them in various aspects of your life.</p>
          <p>For now, let’s start with one that strikes a chord: your romantic relationships.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-2" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(2,3)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual text-left pb-3 pt-5" id="step3">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;">
            <h3 class="centered">As A Caregiver, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Relationship Qualities</span> That Are Within You</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4">
              <img src="../assets/images/relationship.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>Due to your introverted nature, being a home buddy is your type of romance. Whereas other archetypes tend to enjoy parties and going out with others, you are inclined to spend romantic dinners at home and do Netflix afterwards.</p>
              <p>When you are in a relationship, you retain that introverted you. That’s why you’d prefer to stay at home and spent time with your partner instead. It doesn’t mean though, that you won’t love those romantic dates because you do. The point is when you go out, you prefer some sort of privacy.</p>
              <p>The same also holds true in how you express your relationship on social media. Whereas others flaunt their partners and their statuses, <span class="text-orange">you love keeping things lowkey</span>. Be careful though, since your partner may misconstrue this as you being not proud of them. Just let them know your preference to keep things simple and private.</p>
              <p>By prioritizing privacy, you are <span class="text-orange">demanding your need for private space</span>. Meaning, the way you cherish your partner entails engaging in the most intimate of ways without seeking verification and praises from others. Because you are an introvert with a strong sense of self, you won’t be needing those anyway.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Be careful, though. Sometimes others may perceive this as an insecurity. Since you’re not fond of going out there and parading your happiness, people may think that you’re hiding something even when you’re not. If you lack that mental and emotional fortitude, these small talks can create a silent divide that will slowly get in between you and your partner.</p>
          <p>Also, staying too much at home can prevent you from seeing new perspectives. While you are biased towards growing and nurturing relationships in private, don’t forget that going on trips and dates is also a way for the relationship to flourish. As you explore new things in life, better and wider perspectives are unlocked.</p>
          <p>Always remember that this tendency, when used correctly, is a strength, not a weakness. Keeping things in private allows you to protect those that you love from the prying eyes of jealous individuals around you.</p>
          <hr class="dashed">
          <p>Being a Caregiver, it is part of your core nature to nurture others. Since you are born to help others grow, it is only natural to see you in a relationship where you constantly feed your partner that much-needed positivity. Like an anchor that they can rely on, your presence alone is enough to inspire them to move forward, knowing that you always got their back.</p>
          <p>As such, this means <span class="text-orange">nurturing your partner</span> and the relationship by any means necessary. Starting from material ones, you are willing to work night and day to make sure that the basic needs are fulfilled. And when you’re ready, you are also likely to finance your partner in pursuing their dreams or establishing new businesses or streams of income together.</p>
          <p>More importantly, your ability to nurture your partner emotionally and spiritually is just off the charts. With your altruistic nature, you constantly give your best in encouraging and pushing them to keep fighting. While everything may seem to be at odds, you are never afraid to go forth and lead your partner to greatness. Like a parent who believes that their child will succeed, you give off that positive vibe to your partner, solidifying their need for confidence.</p>
          <p>Just be careful, since nurturing others can mistakenly lead them to become overly dependent on you. Without noticing, the relationship can become parasitic instead of mutual. Whereas relationships must work on the premise of mutually beneficial growth, your altruistic tendencies may alter this balance in a negative way.</p>
          <p>Thus, make sure that while you nurture your partner, you also do a regular reality check. This will keep your feet planted on the ground.</p>
          <p>As you know, however, the Caregiver is not just about romance and love. Indeed, there’s another aspect in your life where you as a Caregiver can apply yourself, <span class="username"></span>.</p>
          <p>Without further ado, it’s time to see where you can take yourself in your career.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-3" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(3,4)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step4">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A <span class="archetype">Caregiver</span>, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Potential Career Paths</span></h3>
          </div>
          <p>The Caregiver is a combination of introversion, we-centeredness, intuitiveness, and calmness. This makes up for strong career paths in relation to social service, education, and people management. With their altruistic nature, Caregivers can blossom in these paths. And while these are suggestive of what you can pursue with your strengths, know that you should never limit yourself to them.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/social-worker.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Social Worker</h5>
              <p>With their uniqueness, Caregivers are best suited as social workers. Because they have the natural desire to help others, they’ll find it natural to serve the marginalized.</p>
              <p>As a Caregiver, your gift is compassion and generosity. With these gifts, you can share them with the world by taking up a career that pays you to do so. While social workers aren’t necessarily highly paid, the emotional rewards of their actions are truly unparalleled.</p>
              <p>For instance, social workers are sometimes assigned in the slums where minorities feel the systemic effects of the government. Unable to assert their rights, these minorities are often shortchanged when it comes to equal opportunities and stable starting lines. Instead, they are often challenged to begin from a handicapped starting point.</p>
              <p>Immersing yourself in their situation, you understand what they need in order to grow and flourish. This will require your heart, mind, and soul, as you live out your purpose by being a social worker. And as you dedicate your time, talent, and treasures, you will find purpose and meaning in life.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/school-teacher.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>School Teacher</h5>
              <p>Since Caregivers love to nurture others, becoming a school teacher is definitely within the best options. As a part of the education system, Caregivers will act as guardians and tutors for the nation’s young minds. Caregivers will play a vital role in shaping their growth with the right values and wisdom and practical knowledge.</p>
              <p>As a school teacher, you will unlock the opportunity of earning decently (depending on which country you reside) while serving your mission in life. This may seem underrated for some, or even most, but this is one of the best scenarios for you as a Caregiver. Instead of trapping yourself in some 9-to-5 job that needs to meet market needs, you’ll be contained in a farm-like environment whose ultimate goal is to aid the students’ growth.</p>
              <p>More importantly, being a school teacher also means that you’ll have the chance to truly touch the lives of others. Especially if you’re teaching children, their formative years are at your responsibility, allowing you to practically shape the kind of persons they will become.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>By dedicating yourself to this profession, you will also learn more about life. As you touch the lives of many students and as they reciprocate, later on, you’ll realize the impact of the actions that you make on a daily basis. By doing your best, you get to serve the greater good, especially when you’ve imparted the right mindset to your students.</p>
          <p>As a consequence, this career path allows you to live out your gift of bringing joy and happiness to others. More than becoming an internet icon, this career path will allow you to experience life’s fragility and beauty, a paradox that you understand better than anyone else.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/counselors.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Counselors/Psychologists</h5>
              <p>Apart from Jesters, Caregivers can also be excellent counselors or psychologists. But unlike the Jester, whose main offering is the intricate understanding of life, Caregivers can offer something more – the unparalleled ability to resonate with their patients. Able to feel things out, Caregivers can process the inner struggles of those that seek their help.</p>
              <p>Since Caregivers are we-centered and intuitive, they are inherently interested in understanding the situation of their patients. Instead of simply prescribing medications and mental exercises to their patients, Caregivers will make the extra effort of truly learning about their patient’s situation.</p>
              <p>Given such, they won’t mind as much, even when it can actually be more time-consuming on their end. In most cases, true Caregivers won’t even consider money as a problem. While tending to one’s mental health can truly be costly, Caregivers are willing to set aside this issue, especially for those who can’t afford.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>As a Caregiver who’ll pursue this line of work, you will stop at nothing as you unravel the deepest anxieties and depressions of your patient. Driven by your altruistic nature, your genuine care and concern for them will empower you to break stereotypes and conquer challenges no matter how insurmountable they may seem.</p>
          <p>In effect, your patients will feel loved and cared for. And when they do, bit by bit, you’ll be adding some positive energy to their lives. Empowering them from within, your guidance can lead them to new horizons.</p>
          <p>But while your career prospects certainly glimmer with the hope of prosperity, there are uncomfortable truths about yourself that you will need to face. The first of which will be no more comforting, <span class="username"></span>, and it is this...</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-4" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(4,5)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
